description:
whois() validates user_profile.id for null bytes but not login_name. Both fields are used in downstream Identity struct. Rust Strings can contain null bytes from JSON \u0000 escape. Add same validation to login_name.

Fix: after null-byte check on id, add: if result.user_profile.login_name.contains('\0') { return Err(WhoIsFailed("null byte in login_name".into())); }

Files: crates/kith-tslocal/src/lib.rs whois()
